<title>PHILIPPINES: Meralco board elects former energy chief.</title>
<headline>Meralco board elects former energy chief.</headline>
<dateline>MANILA 1996-10-23</dateline>
<text>
<p>Manila Electric Co said on Wednesday that former energy minister Delfin Lazaro has been elected to its board.</p>
<p>Meralco, the Philippines' largest power distributor, said in a statement that Lazaro was elected at a board meeting on October 21.</p>
<p>Lazaro was energy minister from December 1992 to September 1994 and is credited with helping to solve a crippling power shortage by the commissioning of more than 1,000 megawatts (Mw) of fast-track power plants.</p>
<p>- Manila newsroom 63 2 8418939 fax 8176267</p>
</text>
